    "created_at": "2026-09-25T06:25:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-25T06:25:55Z",
    "body": "Right, <s>display</s> preferred size already takes `multiple` into account when deciding what to do:\n\n> The display size of a [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-select-element) element is the result of applying the [rules for parsing non-negative integers](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers) to the value of the element's [size](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-select-size) attribute, if it has one and parsing it is successful. If applying those rules to the attribute's value is not successful, or if the [size](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-select-size) attribute is absent, then the element's [display size](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-select-size) is 4 if the element's [multiple](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-select-multiple) content attribute is present, and 1 otherwise.\n\nOne complication here is using `attr()` in the user agent style sheet which has completely different parsing rules: #12952. 😕 Not sure how to reconcile that.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
